# logrotate config for the New-IT-System backend application log.
#
# This file is a REPO ARTIFACT, not an installed config. Install it manually:
#   sudo cp deploy/logrotate/new-it-backend /etc/logrotate.d/new-it-backend
# See docs/architecture/logging-system.md for the install + verification steps.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# The backend used to rotate its own log with Python's
# TimedRotatingFileHandler. Production runs `uvicorn --workers 4`, and every
# worker re-imports app.main -> every worker built its own handler, its own fd
# and its own rolloverAt clock, all renaming/unlinking the same path at
# midnight. Measured on prod: 18 of 30 archives contained cross-day data, 25 of
# 30 calendar days were split across >=2 files, and doRollover()'s
# os.remove(dfn) can delete an entire day's archive. The app now uses
# WatchedFileHandler (reopens when the file's inode changes) and rotation is
# delegated here, where exactly one process does it.
#
# WHY EACH DIRECTIVE
# ------------------
# two paths     Production writes backend/logs-prod/, development writes
#               backend/logs/. Both containers lost in-process rotation with
#               the WatchedFileHandler switch, so both need covering. Each path
#               keeps its own independent archive set.
# su root root  The containers run as root, so backend.log is root-owned, while
#               the backend/logs/ directory itself is owned by kcm-trade.
#               logrotate refuses to rotate in a directory whose owner differs
#               from the file owner unless told which user to act as.
# daily         Matches the previous when="midnight" cadence.
# rotate 30     Matches the previous backupCount=30 (30 days retained). This
#               also replaces the manual `find -mtime +30 -delete` cleanup that
#               used to be documented.
# missingok     Dev may be stopped for weeks; a missing backend.log is normal
#               and must not produce a nightly cron error mail.
# notifempty    Don't create an empty archive for a day with no traffic.
# create 0644 root root
#               LOAD-BEARING — do NOT change this to copytruncate.
#               `create` rotates by rename(2), which gives the new backend.log a
#               NEW INODE. That inode change is precisely the signal
#               WatchedFileHandler stat()s for before each emit, and it is what
#               lets all 4 workers follow the rotation independently and
#               atomically. copytruncate keeps the same inode, so the handler
#               would never notice, every worker would keep writing at its old
#               (now huge, sparse) offset, and the scheme silently fails —
#               plus copytruncate has an inherent lost-lines window between the
#               cp and the truncate. Mode/owner mirror what the containers
#               already produce (root:root 0644).
# dateext + dateformat .%Y-%m-%d
#               Reproduces the existing archive names byte for byte
#               (backend.log.2026-07-06), instead of logrotate's default
#               numeric backend.log.1. The 31 existing archives need no
#               migration, the `backend.log*` glob keeps matching, and every
#               grep/tail command in the docs keeps working unchanged.
# dateyesterday logrotate runs shortly after 00:00, so the file being rotated
#               holds YESTERDAY's lines. Without this the archive would be
#               stamped with today's date and every filename would be off by
#               one day.
# nocompress    The old archives are plain text; keeping them uncompressed
#               means `grep backend.log*` still works without zgrep. Disk is
#               not a constraint here (~2MB/day, ~60MB for 30 days per path).
# nocopytruncate
#               Explicit belt-and-braces against a future edit or a global
#               default re-enabling it. See the `create` note above.
# sharedscripts Run pre/postrotate scripts once for the whole path set rather
#               than once per path. There are no scripts today (nothing needs
#               signalling — WatchedFileHandler self-heals), but this makes the
#               intent explicit if one is ever added.

/opt/myproject/New-IT-System/backend/logs-prod/backend.log
/opt/myproject/New-IT-System/backend/logs/backend.log
{
    su root root
    daily
    rotate 30
    missingok
    notifempty
    create 0644 root root
    dateext
    dateyesterday
    dateformat .%Y-%m-%d
    nocompress
    nocopytruncate
    sharedscripts
}
